          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "New since 7061eb6dd1: c901a32544 (#4197 EV-6c part 2) adds `pv discharge check --kani <dir> --baseline <file>` and `pv discharge kani-ratchet` (crates/aprender-contracts-cli/src/commands/discharge_kani.rs, ratchet_down in crates/aprender-contracts/src/kani_assume.rs) plus contracts/kani-assume-baseline.json (181 assumes across 27 files). Ran the tests myself rather than trusting the commit message's numbers: cargo test -p aprender-contracts --lib kani_assume -> 15/15 passed; cargo test -p aprender-contracts-cli --test pvl_kani_assume -> 9/9 passed; cargo test -p aprender-contracts-cli --lib discharge -> 25/25 passed. All three match the commit message exactly. Clap wiring (lean_dir now Option<PathBuf> with required_unless_present=\"kani\", --kani conflicts_with_all the Lean-only flags) is exercised by the_lean_arms_are_refused_with_kani, and ratchet_down's min(was,now)-per-file / never-admits-a-new-file semantics are exercised by ratchet_down_only_ever_lowers_and_never_admits_a_new_file and the_ratchet_cannot_launder_a_rise. No defect found in this new surface."
          },
          "locations": [
            { "physicalLocation": { "artifactLocation": { "uri": "crates/aprender-contracts-cli/src/commands/discharge_kani.rs" }, "region": { "startLine": 1 } } },
            { "physicalLocation": { "artifactLocation": { "uri": "crates/aprender-contracts/src/kani_assume.rs" }, "region": { "startLine": 270 } } }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "command": ["cargo", "test", "-p", "aprender-contracts", "--lib", "kani_assume"],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "failure_scenario": "Had the ratchet's downward-only semantics been wrong (e.g. admitting a new risen file, or writing the measured/higher value instead of the old/lower one for a risen file), the kani::assume ratchet could be laundered by the same commit that raised it; the three test suites above (15+9+25 = 49 tests) exercise exactly that boundary and all pass."
          }
